dsv41 patch 0055 (20.10.2026): draft mode per request: sampled drafts for code/JSON, greedy drafts for prose.
Base: vllm/v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dspark/speculator.py of image v5.
Why: probabilistic drafting with block verification raised tokens per round at T=1 for code and JSON (+3.95 % overall,
code at 1 stream 3.70 -> 4.05), but its full-vocabulary draft path costs ~1 ms a round and prose did not gain.
How: only requests in the full-window regime of patch 0047 (scheduled drafts == the batch's k, i.e. accepted-draft
average >= VLLM_DSV41_AK_HI: code, JSON) draft by sampling; the others draft greedily, and their cached draft
distribution becomes one-hot at the drafted token (Triton kernel, skips padding rows). The rejection sampler then
verifies those rows exactly like greedy drafts (q(x) = 1, residual = p without x), also under block verification.
Needs draft_sample_method=probabilistic and VLLM_DSPARK_LOCAL_ARGMAX=0 (we ran it with rejection_sample_method=block).
Measured (20.10.2026, GB10, 2000 MHz, image v6, against the production setup): T=1 geometric mean +0.75 %, tokens per
round +3.7 %, code at 1 stream +5.0 %, prose at 1 stream -1.6 %, JSON at 4 streams -5.1 %; suite code 88.6 -> 99.1, prose
54.0 -> 52.3 tok/s; with a 0047 margin of 0.5 on top -0.47 %. Not adopted.
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_HYBRID_DRAFT=1 (default off).

